{"id":"odu-mcp-rerun-doc","parent":"oduc-agent","ord":"a0","title":"odu: the MCP hides its single-lane retry","todo":true,"desc":"When one lane of a multi-platform run fails, the right move is to re-run that one lane — it works on a LIVE run, alongside the still-running sibling, cancelling nothing. The tool that does it, `node_rerun`, ships with NO description at all: an agent sees a bare `id` parameter and no hint of what it is for.\n\nMeanwhile `run`'s own description says \"one run per checkout\" and offers `supersede` prominently — which restarts the whole run and kills the other lanes. So the cheap correct operation is invisible and the expensive destructive one is the documented one. An agent reasoning from the tool surface concludes it must throw away a running darwin lane to retry a flaky linux one; that happened, and a person had to correct it.\n\nWanted: a real description on `node_rerun` (what it does, that it works mid-run, that nothing else is cancelled), a cross-reference from `run`/`supersede` saying this is the way to retry one lane, and the same correction wherever agents read odu's docs. Small change; the difference between an agent doing the right thing by itself and wasting a six-minute lane.","created":"2026-08-31T16:53:16-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T16:54:06-04:00","custom":{"from":"juspay/odu#34 (srid, 2026-06-19), moved here 2026-08-31 when odu's issues came to the vault"}}
{"id":"odu-green-exit-nonzero","parent":"oduc-runs","ord":"a0","title":"odu: a green run can still exit non-zero","doing":true,"started":"2026-08-31T16:55:33-04:00","desc":"Every node passes, the green statuses post — and the process still exits non-zero, because something failed while tearing down the remote ssh connection after the verdict was already in. Whatever launched the run sees a failure that did not happen, and scripts, CI wrappers and agents all key off that exit code.\n\nLIKELY ALREADY FIXED, needs one honest confirmation: odu#93 (merged 2026-08-29) made a dying transport error a single node instead of taking the coordinator down with it, which is the same teardown seam. Every odu run this vault has driven since then has exited cleanly. The remaining work is to confirm it rather than assume — reproduce the old shape (kill a lane's ssh at the end of a green run) and see what the exit code is; if it is 0, close this with the evidence.","created":"2026-08-31T16:53:16-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T17:10:46-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-grok","brief":"briefs/odu-green-exit.md","dispatched":"2026-08-31T17:00:00-04:00","from":"juspay/odu#18 (srid, 2026-06-11), moved here 2026-08-31","kolu-terminal":"958365fa","merge":"merge-auto","odu-worktree":".worktrees/green-exit","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/odu/pull/95","repo":"repo-odu","tier":"ordinary"}}
{"id":"odu-recipe-groups","parent":"oduc-recipes","ord":"a0","title":"odu: name a group of recipes and run it","todo":true,"desc":"To run part of a pipeline today you must spell out every recipe by name — there is no way to say \"the build group\" or \"the fast checks\". Wanted: define a named group once, then select it with one word, from the command line and through the agent interface alike.\n\nWhy it matters more for agents than for people: a person can keep a list in their head, but an agent has to know and repeat every recipe name to scope a run, and gets it wrong or gives up and runs everything.","created":"2026-08-31T16:53:16-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T16:54:07-04:00","custom":{"from":"juspay/odu#16 (srid, 2026-06-11), moved here 2026-08-31"}}
{"id":"odu-bun-attach","parent":"oduc-runtime","ord":"a0","title":"odu: should the attach face move to bun? #needs-brainstorm","todo":true,"desc":"A decision record, not a task: should odu leave node+tsx for bun, mainly to unlock OpenTUI for the attach face?\n\nWhat the June research established. odu is on node by packaging convenience, not by a considered choice. OpenTUI's native renderer needs bun's FFI — under node it throws — though it has since started running on current-line node behind an experimental flag, which nixpkgs' LTS node does not have. So bun is the viable path today and node may be the path in six to twelve months. The real risk of a full port is that bun's weakest area (child processes, stdio teardown) is exactly odu's core competency, and unit tests on node would not catch it. The pull beyond widgets is that kolu's reactive hooks are Solid-only, so an OpenTUI+Solid terminal could share view code with a browser observer.\n\nThe recommendation on file, still the sensible one: do not port the runner. Prototype the ATTACH FACE on bun — read-only, no process supervision, smallest blast radius — and decide the rest afterwards. Cheapest first step either way: re-probe OpenTUI's renderer under current node with the experimental FFI flag and see how real that path has become.","created":"2026-08-31T16:53:16-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T16:54:07-04:00","custom":{"from":"juspay/odu#27 (srid, 2026-06-12), moved here 2026-08-31 — the research and its recommendation preserved"}}
