{"id":"lane-oge-review","parent":"odu-green-exit-nonzero","ord":"a3","title":"review: claude-opus","done":"2026-08-31T17:17:21-04:00","started":"2026-08-31T17:10:46-04:00","worked":395,"after":["lane-oge-fix"],"created":"2026-08-31T17:10:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T17:17:21-04:00","custom":{"kolu-terminal":"b748f4fb","musts":"1","reviewer":"agent-claude-opus","shoulds":"1","verdict":"MUST: odu.test.ts:534 is a vacuous pin — named \"teardown is not an input\" but teardown never appears, and the iff misses the cancelled and unsettled arms (proved by mutation: drop the cancelled clause and it still passes). SHOULD: the kill-after-green e2e has no positive evidence the death was observed — under --linger printVerdict never runs, so an unnoticing idle-reap satisfies every assertion. Also corrected the central claim: teardown DOES write node statuses via onDead→terminalizePlatformNodes; the real invariant is that an ok node is immune to a post-verdict lane death, kept by four guards, one in @kolu/surface-remote (which is why only a black-box kill can pin it). The EPIPE/sealed-log greps verified NOT vacuous. Comment 5484711319."}}
